<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  A wave, drawn as a wave.

  Not a line of dots along a curve - that reads as a dotted rule, which is what this
  first attempt was. This is a shape with an edge: a crest line that rises and falls, and
  a body of water under it that is thickest beneath the crest and thins to nothing at
  both ends.

  The dots are what makes the shape, and the thing that does it is their **size**. Each dot
  is sized by how far it sits from the nearer of the two edges, so the wave is solid through
  the middle and frays at the boundaries - which is how a halftone reads as tone. Uniform
  dots could only ever have drawn an outline.

  27 columns by 14 rows over the middle of the 108 viewport, which is the only part of an
  adaptive icon every launcher is obliged to show.
-->
